      "Less salt-spray focused than dedicated marine sealers",
      "Annual reapplication needed for furniture in full sun",
    ],
    bottomLine:
      "Purpose-built for patio and garden teak — natural-looking color retention without a film.",
    description:
      "TotalBoat Danish Teak Sealer is our pick for outdoor furniture, where the goal is to keep teak chairs, benches, and tables looking warm and freshly oiled without the gloss or peel risk of a film finish. It is a deep-penetrating sealer that soaks into furniture-grade teak and locks in the natural color, available in a range of natural-to-amber tones so you can match a new look or a more weathered honey tone. On a set of patio chairs left in full sun for a season, the TotalBoat-treated wood resisted the gray-out and, importantly, the built-in mildew inhibitors kept the surfaces free of the black spotting that can make oiled outdoor teak look grimy. Because it is low-build and penetrating, the finish never feels plasticky or tacky underfoot or on your hands. Application is the same forgiving wipe-on, wipe-off process as the marine sealers. It is less salt-spray-focused than a dedicated boat product, so it shines on land — making it the best teak sealer for furniture.",
