      "Widely available and inexpensive per coat",
      "Excellent on indoor teak and fine furniture",
      "Builds a soft luster with successive coats",
    ],
    cons: [
      "An oil, not a sealer — needs frequent reapplication",
      "Can promote mildew on outdoor teak in damp climates",
    ],
    bottomLine:
      "A superb nourishing oil for indoor teak — but understand it is an oil, not a long-term outdoor sealer.",
    description:
      "Watco Teak Oil is the classic teak oil, and it earns a spot here because so many people cross-shop teak oil and teak sealer — they are not the same thing. Watco is a penetrating oil that soaks into the grain, nourishes the wood, and brings out a gorgeous warm, hand-rubbed luster that genuinely looks richer than any sealer can. On indoor teak — dining tables, trim, fine furniture — it is hard to beat, and it is cheap and available everywhere. The honest caveat is the one that matters most: an oil is not a sealer. It does not contain the heavy UV blockers a sealer does, so on outdoor teak it weathers away in weeks to a couple of months and needs frequent reapplication. Worse, in damp or humid climates the oil itself can feed mildew, leaving black spotting on patio and marine teak. Use Watco where it excels — indoors and on protected furniture — and reach for a true sealer outdoors.",
  },
  {
    id: "starbrite-premium-teak-oil",
    name: "Star Brite Premium Teak Oil",
    category: "Penetrating Teak Oil",
