      "Cabot Australian Timber Oil is the heavy-duty option on our list, formulated for dense, oily exotic hardwoods like teak, ipe, and mahogany that resist ordinary finishes. It is a heavier-bodied oil finish than the thin marine teak sealers, carrying a robust load of UV-blocking pigment that gives outstanding color retention on horizontal, high-traffic surfaces — which makes it a favorite for teak and exotic-wood decking rather than delicate furniture. In testing it delivered genuine water repellency, with rain beading on the surface long after bare teak had soaked through, and it held its warm tone through a full season of sun. The trade-offs are honest: because it is a heavier penetrating finish, surface prep and even application matter more than with a wipe-on sealer, and the pigment can darken teak more than a clear penetrating product. If your project is a teak deck or a hard-used hardwood surface that needs real water protection and lasting color, this is the best teak sealer-style finish for the job.",
